IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-validity`
IMPORT `g2-second-schedule`
IMPORT `g2-tests-fixtures`

-- g2-tests-second-schedule.l4: tests of the Second Schedule as data and as an engine.
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of the Schedule (inputs/law.wiki, checked against the gazette pages 201 to 205)
-- and from the readings registered in g2-second-schedule.l4, BEFORE any module was run; the day counts of the experience
-- scenarios come from the Python calendar (work/g2/oracle-style script), not from the L4.  A failing assertion is a finding.
-- The expectations of the readings NOT taken, asserted as if they were the answer, are in g2-tests-red.l4.

GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
      applicant IS AN Applicant
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the item numbers under` reading `for a` kind `by` applicant `made on` day MEANS
    map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number`)
        (`Second Schedule — the items that apply under` reading `to` (`an application for a` kind `by` applicant `made on` day) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests`)

GIVEN kind IS A `Licence kind`
      applicant IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the item numbers for a` kind `by` applicant MEANS
    `the item numbers under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `for a` kind `by` applicant `made on` `the usual application day`

GIVEN items IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the item numbers of` items MEANS
    map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number`) items

GIVEN item IS A `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ceiling of the first entry of column B of` item MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the ceiling on the hours of` (at (item's `column B: any one of`) 0)

GIVEN item IS A `Second Schedule item`
GIVETH A Certificate
`the certificate conferred by the first entry of column B of` item MEANS
    CONSIDER at (item's `column B: any one of`) 0
    WHEN `training of up to` ceiling certificate THEN certificate
    WHEN `column B: the certificate itself` certificate THEN certificate
    WHEN `column B: no further requirement` THEN `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`

-- Guard on the named readings: each alternative differs from the reading taken in exactly the one field it is named for (the readings are built
-- positionally, and a slip in the order would otherwise go unseen).
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if the booleans differ:` a `and` b MEANS
    IF a EQUALS b THEN 0 ELSE 1

GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` reading MEANS
        `one if the booleans differ:` (reading's `an ungraded Division certificate in column A reaches every grade`) `and` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `an ungraded Division certificate in column A reaches every grade`)
    PLUS `one if the booleans differ:` (reading's `item 1 applies only where there is no prior training or experience at all`) `and` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `item 1 applies only where there is no prior training or experience at all`)
    PLUS `one if the booleans differ:` (reading's `item 1 also applies to the holder of a certificate its own column B names`) `and` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `item 1 also applies to the holder of a certificate its own column B names`)
    PLUS `one if the booleans differ:` (reading's `registration alone also reaches the applicant who completed the programme`) `and` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `registration alone also reaches the applicant who completed the programme`)
    PLUS (IF reading's `the days that make a year of cumulative experience` EQUALS `the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `the days that make a year of cumulative experience` THEN 0 ELSE 1)
    PLUS `one if the booleans differ:` (reading's `work on the day of the application counts`) `and` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `work on the day of the application counts`)
    PLUS `one if the booleans differ:` (reading's `overlapping periods of work are added, not counted once`) `and` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `overlapping periods of work are added, not counted once`)
    PLUS `one if the booleans differ:` (reading's `a licence named in column A counts although it is no longer in force`) `and` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `a licence named in column A counts although it is no longer in force`)
    PLUS (IF reading's `how a Division certificate of the grade sought is read` EQUALS `the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `how a Division certificate of the grade sought is read` THEN 0 ELSE 1)

#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading with the ungraded certificate rows reaching every grade (FS1)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading with item 1 only for applicants with no prior training or experience at all (FS2a)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading with item 1 also open to the holder of a certificate its column B names (FS2b)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading with registration alone reaching every registered applicant (FS3)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` (`the reading with a year of cumulative experience counted in days (FS7a)` 366) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading with work on the day of the application counted (FS7b)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading with overlapping periods of work added (FS7c)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading with a licence named in column A counting although it has lapsed (FS9)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of fields in which the reading differs from the reading taken` `the reading with a Division certificate of a higher grade also meeting item 1 (FS11)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`the reading with a year of cumulative experience counted in days (FS7a)` 366)'s `the days that make a year of cumulative experience` EQUALS 366
#ASSERT `the reading of the Second Schedule taken`'s `the days that make a year of cumulative experience` EQUALS 365

§ `Tests — the Second Schedule as data`

-- Seventeen items: Part A three, Part B six, Part C eight (inputs/law.wiki lines 568 to 695).
#ASSERT count `the Second Schedule` EQUALS 17
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the part: the licence kind it leads to` EQUALS `grade 1 licence`) `the Second Schedule`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the part: the licence kind it leads to` EQUALS `grade 2 licence`) `the Second Schedule`) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the part: the licence kind it leads to` EQUALS `grade 3 licence`) `the Second Schedule`) EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the item numbers of` (filter (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the part: the licence kind it leads to` EQUALS `grade 2 licence`) `the Second Schedule`) EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6

