#ASSERT `Second Schedule — the hours the applicant must complete under` (`column B: the certificate itself` `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `Second Schedule — the ceiling on the hours of` `column B: no further requirement`
-- The alternative: "up to N" read as exactly N.
#ASSERT `Second Schedule (up to N read as exactly N) — the hours the applicant must complete under` (`training of up to` 350 `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`) EQUALS 350
#ASSERT `Second Schedule (up to N read as exactly N) — the hours the applicant must complete under` `column B: no further requirement` EQUALS 0
-- Column B of items: the requirements, and a named refusal where column B states none (the wiki's Part C item 4).
#ASSERT count (`Second Schedule — the requirements in column B of` (LIST `Second Schedule, Part A, item 1`)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT REFUSED `Second Schedule — the requirements in column B of` (LIST `Second Schedule, Part C, item 4, as the wiki prints it`)

§ `Tests — Part A, grade 1 licence: which items apply (application on the usual day, 1.9.2026)`

-- A1 is the default item of its Part (fork FS2): no prior training or experience, or none that another item of the Part fits.
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing` EQUALS LIST 1
-- A holder of a 3-unit Ministry of Education certificate: no other item of Part A fits, so the default item applies, and its
-- option (2) is the certificate itself (A1(2)).
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`)) EQUALS LIST 1
-- A holder of a 5-unit certificate seeking a grade 1 licence, a youth school certificate, a grade 1 licence already held: no item of Part A names them, so the default item applies.
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`)) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a certificate of the Training Division vocational school for youth`)) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only the licences` (LIST (`an ordinary grade 1 licence granted on` (YMD 2025 1 1)))) EQUALS LIST 1

-- A3: a certificate in refrigeration and air-conditioning studies from the Training Division.  Part A names no graded certificate, so a Division certificate
-- reaches A3 unless it is the grade 1 certificate that item 1 of Part A itself confers (D1, fork FS10: that holder has met item 1) - the ungraded certificate, and the higher grades (FS11).
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated`)) EQUALS LIST 3
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the item numbers for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) EQUALS LIST 3

-- A2, the experience item.  KIND B (backwards) windows: a year of cumulative experience within the three years before the application
-- (1.9.2023 to 31.8.2026), or three years within the seven years before it (1.9.2019 to 31.8.2026); a year taken as 365 days, so
-- three years are 1095 days (fork FS7).
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`974 days of work from 1.1.2024` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2024 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 8 31)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`365 days of work to 31.8.2026` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2025 9 1) `to` (YMD 2026 8 31)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`364 days of work to 31.8.2026` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2025 9 2) `to` (YMD 2026 8 31)
-- 31.8.2023 to 29.8.2024 is 365 days, but the window opens on 1.9.2023, so 364 days count: the period is clipped to the window.
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`work from 31.8.2023 to 29.8.2024` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2023 8 31) `to` (YMD 2024 8 29)
-- A period that ends on the application day itself: the window ends the day before (fork FS7b).
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`work from 2.9.2025 to the application day 1.9.2026` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2025 9 2) `to` (YMD 2026 9 1)
-- Two overlapping periods: 303 days counted once, 484 added.
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`two overlapping periods of work in the year to 30.6.2026` MEANS LIST (`a period of work from` (YMD 2025 9 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30)), (`a period of work from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30))
-- Exactly 1095 days (2.1.2020 to 31.12.2022, all in the seven year window and none in the three year window), and 1094.
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`1095 days of work from 2.1.2020` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2020 1 2) `to` (YMD 2022 12 31)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
`1094 days of work from 3.1.2020` MEANS LIST `a period of work from` (YMD 2020 1 3) `to` (YMD 2022 12 31)

