§ `Tests — the three-year note of column C (kind C, trap T7)`

-- Three years after the commencement day 16.7.2025 end on 16.7.2028 (Interpretation Law s 10(b); a Sunday), inside the period.
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C — the last day of the three years beginning on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C — the experience items are in force on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) (YMD 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT NOT `Second Schedule column C — the experience items are in force on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) (YMD 2028 7 17)
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C — the experience items are in force on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) (YMD 2025 7 16)
-- The commencement day is the first day the note's items are in force (fork FS8): no earlier day is tested.
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C — the experience items are in force on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) (YMD 2025 7 15)
-- FS8 (kind V of a provision), the alternative: Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied.  16.7.2028 is a Sunday: with Sunday a rest day the last day is Monday 17.7.2028.
GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`a calendar with Sunday 16 July 2028` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2028 7 16)
GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`a calendar with no rest days at all` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C (Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied) — the last day of the three years beginning on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, with` `a calendar with Sunday 16 July 2028` EQUALS YMD 2028 7 17
#ASSERT `Second Schedule column C (Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied) — the last day of the three years beginning on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, with` `a calendar with no rest days at all` EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16

