§ `Tests — the Division certificate of the grade sought (forks FS10 and FS11, defect D1 of 2026-10-14)`

-- Expected values below come from the Schedule's rows and the repair ruling: item 1 of each Part is "training of up to 350/480/720 hours conferring a final
-- certificate of grade 1/2/3", so the holder of that certificate has completed it; rows A3, B5(1) and C6 are for the holder of the lesser, ungraded certificate.

GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
      applicant IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A LIST OF `Second Schedule item`
`the items under` reading `for a` kind `by` applicant MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the items that apply under` reading `to` (`an application for a` kind `by` applicant `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests`

GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
      applicant IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A LIST OF `Requirement of the Second Schedule`
`the entries of column B under` reading `for a` kind `by` applicant MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `column B: any one of`) (`the items under` reading `for a` kind `by` applicant))

-- Taken: the holder of the certificate of the grade sought is in item 1 alone, in every Part.
#ASSERT `the item numbers under` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`) `for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `made on` `the usual application day` EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the item numbers under` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`) `for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `made on` `the usual application day` EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the item numbers under` (`the reading of the Second Schedule taken`) `for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day` EQUALS LIST 1
-- Item 1 as it reads for that holder: column B gains the entry "the certificate itself" for the certificate held; the Schedule's printed entries stay.
#ASSERT `the entries of column B under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) EQUALS LIST (`training of up to` 350 `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`), (`column B: the certificate itself` `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`), (`column B: the certificate itself` `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)
#ASSERT `the entries of column B under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) EQUALS LIST (`training of up to` 480 `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`), (`column B: the certificate itself` `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`), (`column B: the certificate itself` `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)
#ASSERT `the entries of column B under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) EQUALS LIST (`training of up to` 720 `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`), (`column B: the certificate itself` `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)
-- For an applicant who holds no such certificate, item 1 is returned exactly as the Schedule prints it.
#ASSERT `the items under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing` EQUALS LIST `Second Schedule, Part A, item 1`
#ASSERT `the items under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing` EQUALS LIST `Second Schedule, Part B, item 1`
#ASSERT `the items under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing` EQUALS LIST `Second Schedule, Part C, item 1`
